  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/... \n\nThe long term forecast remains dry and seasonal. Ensemble guidance\ncontinues to show a dry positively-tilted trough dropping through\nthe area at the end of the week, ahead of a strong ridge spreading\ninto much of the west. Guidance also shows a cutoff low forming\nsouth of the ridge over the eastern Pacific, west of the Baja\nPeninsula. From here the models diverge a bit. A majority of the\nGEFS members bring the cutoff low up into the Desert Southwest,\ndrawing some moisture up with it. However, the rest of the global\nensemble guidance leans toward a much weaker cutoff low, with the\nDesert Southwest remaining dominated by ridging. Latest NBM PoPs\nthrough the long term forecast remain under 5% across the local\narea. Temperatures late-week through this weekend should warm a\nfew degrees, back to around normal as the ridge builds over the\nWest. Lower desert highs are forecast to be in the upper 70s to\nlower 80s. Breezy northerly winds are likely to develop heading\ninto the end of this week and weekend as surface high pressure\nbuilds over the Great Basin and Rockies, below the upper level\nridge, but wind magnitudes do not look to reach advisory level.",
